==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|belwen}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|bylgian}}, ultimately from the {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} base {{m|ine-pro|*bʰel-||to sound, roar}}, cognate with {{m|ang|belg||leather bag}}, {{m|ang|bellan||to roar}}, {{m|ang|blāwan||to blow}}. Cognate with German {{m|de|bellen||to bark}} and Russian {{m|ru|бле́ять||baa, bleat}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/ˈbɛloʊ/|lang=en}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈbɛləʊ/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɛləʊ|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-bellow.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
{{examples-right|examples={{audio|Elkbellow.ogg|The bellow of an [[elk]]|lang=en}}}}

# the deep [[roar]] of a large animal, or any similar loud noise

